"epo"><addressbook><name>KANDA MASAHIDE</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KASHIMA MITUHIRO</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>MITUSHIMA KOJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HARA, SADAAKI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KANDA, MASAHIDE</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KASHIMA, MITUHIRO</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>MITUSHIMA, KOJI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A seal structure, comprising a sliding member (2), a supporting member (1) slidably storing the sliding member, and a seal ring (5) provided between the sliding member (2) and the supporting member (1), the seal ring (5) being formed of a lip part (10) on which a hydraulic oil pressure acts and a heel part (11) which supports an acted pressure, whereby, because an annular pressure receiving area between the inner and outer peripheries of the lip part (10) is formed smaller than an annular supporting area between the inner and outer peripheries of the heel part (11), a pressure acting on the ring seal is reduced by reducing the pressure receiving area of the lip part smaller than the supporting area of the heel part so that the heel part is prevented from being deformed to the sliding surface side.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne une structure d'étanchéité comprenant un élément coulissant (2), un élément de support (1) renfermant de manière coulissante l'élément coulissant et une bague d'étanchéité (5) venant entre l'élément coulissant (2) et l'élément de support (1), la bague d'étanchéité (5) étant formée d'une partie fourchue (10) sur laquelle est exercée une pression d'huile hydraulique et d'une partie pleine (11) supportant une pression exercée. Comme la zone recevant la pression annulaire entre les pourtours interne et externe de la partie fourchue (10) est plus petite que la zone de support annulaire entre les pourtours interne et externe de la partie pleine (11), une pression exercée sur la bague d'étanchéité est réduite grâce à la réduction de la zone de réception de la pression de la partie fourchue plus petite que la zone de support de la partie pleine de telle sorte que cette dernière ne soit pas déformée vers le côté de la surface coulissante.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>